<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong extends flat presale period to 15 months.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong extends flat presale period to 15 months.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong government said on Wednesday it would extend the presale period for private flats to 15 months from the current 12 months in a bid to bring supply into the market more quickly.  </p>
<p>Housing Secretary Dominic Wong told reporters the move would bring an estimated 5,000 flats to the market earlier.</p>
<p>Wong said the presale period for government-subsidised flats would be extended to 24 months from between 12 and 18 months at present.</p>
</text>
